# Code Style

## Typing & components

- Strict TypeScript — no `any`; explicit return types on functions
- Functional components only; prefer `React.JSX.Element` return type
- Default export PascalCase components; hooks `useX` camelCase
- Props: named `interface ComponentProps { ... }`
- Files match export: `ComponentName.tsx`, `useCustomHook.ts`
- Types in `types/`; constants `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`; config objects camelCase

## Preferred screen pattern

```typescript
export default function ScreenName(): React.JSX.Element {
  const [state, setState] = useState<Type>(initialValue);
  useEffect(() => { /* ... */ }, [deps]);
  return <View>{/* ... */}</View>;
}
```

## Import order

1. React / React Native  
2. Third-party (Expo, Firebase, etc.)  
3. Local components  
4. Hooks  
5. Types, constants, utilities  

## Styling & comments

- `StyleSheet.create()` at file bottom; colors from `constants/theme.ts`
- Screen containers: `SafeAreaView` from `react-native-safe-area-context`
- Gradients: `expo-linear-gradient`
- Prefer self-documenting names; comment complex logic, workarounds, Firebase shape expectations
- JSDoc on reused exported hooks/functions; `// ======` section headers for large files
